    <a href="#content">Skip to the content</a>
    <main id="content" tabindex="-1">
      <h1>Flowfin</h1>
      <p>Flowfin is a set of Jellyfin plugins for a server somebody else runs.</p>
      <p>The clients this project means to build are one genuinely native client per platform, sharing a core between them. None of them is released, so there is nothing here to download and no page describing one as though there were.</p>
      <p>The table below is the whole list, and it is rendered from the roster rather than written here. Adding a plugin is a row in that file; nothing on this page has to be edited for it to appear, and nothing here can say a different thing about a plugin from what the roster says.</p>
      <p>What a state word declares is what is true before anything is published. It is the floor rather than the answer, because whether a plugin ships is a fact about published releases and not an opinion a row may hold.</p>
      <p>This file carries the title, the sentence a search result shows and the paragraphs above the table. What it may not carry is a claim about whether something is available: that is a value the build reads, so the page cannot go on saying it after it has stopped being true.</p>
      <h2>The plugins, and what state each one is in</h2>
      <p>6 rows, read from the roster this repository carries. What each plugin has published was read on 2026-01-02, and the state below is computed from that rather than declared: a row says what is true before anything is published, and a finished release raises it.</p>
      <table>
        <tr>
          <th>Plugin</th>
          <th>What it does</th>
          <th>State</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><a href="/plugins/a/">a</a></td>
          <td>The shortest identifier a row may carry</td>
          <td>In build-up</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><a href="/plugins/a-row-whose-identifier-is-as-long-as-one-here-ever-gets/">a-row-whose-identifier-is-as-long-as-one-here-ever-gets</a></td>
          <td>The longest identifier a row may carry, which is where a table cell and a page address stop being comfortable</td>
          <td>Shell only</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><a href="/plugins/markup/">markup</a></td>
          <td>A sentence carrying &lt;b&gt;markup&lt;/b&gt;, an &amp; ampersand, a &#34;quotation&#34; and an &#39;apostrophe&#39;, so that a page rendering it as markup is a page this file catches</td>
          <td>In build-up</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><a href="/plugins/outside-ascii/">outside-ascii</a></td>
          <td>A sentence with an em dash — a “curly quotation” and the name Zoë in it, none of which is ASCII</td>
          <td>Shell only</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><a href="/plugins/one-prerelease/">one-prerelease</a></td>
          <td>A row with a single prerelease published, which is the sentence written in the singular</td>
          <td>In build-up</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><a href="/plugins/declared-shell-and-shipping/">declared-shell-and-shipping</a></td>
          <td>A row declaring the shell state for a repository that has published a finished release, which is the disagreement the state is computed to settle</td>
          <td>Ships</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
      
    </main>
